{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations","id":389504,"title":"Supernatural Relations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T23:52:46-08:00","id":389504,"title":"Supernatural Relations","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Okay so I was wondering if there was any pregathered information about the different races of the World of Darkness (Specifically oWoD) and how they interact with each other. There is obvious things like the Garou and Kindred hating each other. But I was wondering how all the supernatural beings regard each other.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Like, do Demons work with the fae on occasion, do they hate the kindred due to Cain. Do Wraiths and Mummies hang out on occasion? I am just hoping there is something out there so that I don't need to spend time reading through the Core Book and companions of every single oWOD system books.<br /> <br /> Also I don't see any sections for Demon:The Fallen. Does it just not have any support or something? Has it been abandoned completely?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4902-letsgetspooky","name":"LetsGetSpooky","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T00:48:55-08:00","id":389525,"title":"","content":"I'm not as up to date on the Amenti-Mummies, but the Shemsu-Heru from 1st and 2nd Ed Mummy were pretty much up in the other supernaturals' business. <br /> <br /> Mummies and <b>Kindred</b> tend to have cool relations to one another. Mummies seek to establish and uphold Ma'at - cosmic balance and justice - while the Kindred tend to be in it for themselves. Furthermore, the inherent abilities that the Kindred condition tend to mess with Ma'at. The Blood Bond creates a perverse addiction that feels very much like love to the victim of the bond. The Kiss too is a very addicting experience, and can leave mental scars on a blood doll's psyche. And yet, there is hope of salvation for the Kindred through Golconda. <br /> <br /> A mummy could become a mentor to a Kindred seeking Golconda, aiding the vampire in how to avoid the traps of the Beast. The vampire in turn is ageless, just like the mummy. While all of the mummy's mortal companions will eventually pass on, the Kindred will always be around, lessening the feeling of being alienated from the constantly changing world.<br /> <br /> The Kindred also make good catspaws in the war against the servants of Apophis and its servants, the Followers of Set. Most Kindred fear and despise the Setites. The mummies, who know the Setites all too well, could secretly feed information about the Setites to the Kindred, and subtly encourage the Kindred to oust the Serpents from their domains, and break their webs of corruption. <br /> <br /> Obviously, I've not yet touched upon the other supernaturals, but I'll come to them eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T04:38:01-08:00","id":389685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LetsGetSpooky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations#post389504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Also I don't see any sections for Demon:The Fallen. Does it just not have any support or something? Has it been abandoned completely?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You'll notice there're no sections for Changeling: the Dreaming or Hunter: the Reckoning either. It's not a matter of not being supported; it's that the cWOD games get a dedicated section around the time their 20th anniversary edition gets a Kickstarter, and Changeling, Hunter and Demon aren't at that stage (Hunter and Demon being several years off).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T07:19:20-08:00","id":389809,"title":"","content":"Mage interactions with other supernaturals can range from 'kill on sight' up through 'pacify and study' all the way to 'cherish and protect'. Just going to toss some off-the-top ideas out here, but keep in mind that with mages specifically it will <i><u>depend highly on the individuals</u></i> involved. <br /> <br /> \u200bHere are some general stereotypes:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Akashics hate Vampires (and most Demons) and sometimes actively hunt them. They deeply respect most shape-changers (as they strictly abide by their intended purposes), but especially the Stargazers - whom they consider ancient allies and will pay some respect out of the box.<br /> <br /> Euthanatos deal with Wraiths often. They are somewhat fascinated by mummies, and do not hate them at all! (Mummies return to the wheel and reincarnate in a special way, sort of like rock stars for the Euthies.) They despise Vampires as an affront to the great Wheel, and will almost always try to kill them.<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers deal with Spirits often, and will fight Demons with much fervor. They have some minor interactions with Garou, and while it doesn't always go well there is some potential. They are great friends with many of the Bastet, and respect all of the Fera.<br /> <br /> Hollow Ones are hard to generalize about, but in my world they often see vampires as sort of a romantic or wistful idea. Yes, this causes trouble (in my world).<br /> <br /> Celestial Chorus are extremely 'vigilant', although what is dangerous they may disagree on. There are a lot of Chorister concepts involved with 'Vampire Hunting' or 'Demon Hunting'. They are out there doing God's work.<br /> <br /> Cultists will fight against anything or anyone who tries to impose their desires onto another. This will vary, but they aren't typically the 'hold a grudge' type.<br /> <br /> Sons of Ether / Virtual Adepts generally don't have any major stereotypes for other supernaturals. Maybe they just don't have the history for it.<br /> <br /> The Order of Hermes... ahh, well... remember when I mentioned 'pacify and study'? Their hubris is generally so institutionalized that there is nothing they wouldn't see as an opportunity for greater knowledge or lore. They could literally go any way with any other supernatural group.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:42:45-08:00","id":389894,"title":"","content":"Garou and Fera, a general perspective.<br /> <br /> Vampires are an affront to life, but seeking them out is usually a lot of trouble, so they typically only make them go from undead to all dead if they don't have anything pressing on hand, which is not a common occurrence.<br /> <br /> Mages are caern-robbers and affronts to the order intended by Gaia, who know just enough to be really dangerous to what the Garou and Fera typically safeguard. Because Changers typically, again, have more pressing business, they generally don't mess with them unless a caern, wallow, etc. is in danger, in which case they will tear the Mage's arms off and stuff them down the willworker's mouth, if said willworker is lucky.<br /> <br /> Wraiths other than Risen don't tend to interact with most Garou very often. Those Risen that do were usually killed by Garou, and you know what that entails.<br /> <br /> Changelings are capricious bastards that might aid, hinder or worse. Not to be trusted, but generally not to be killed on sight unless they're particularly bad fae.<br /> <br /> Imbued get treated like normal, mortal hunters (which is to say, usually ending up with a terrible case of being mauled), only with more general paranoia about how they manage to accomplish various feats and why, leading to many existential conversations between dealing with their actual business.<br /> <br /> Demons would likely be seen as just another type of bane, assuming that W:tA ever acknowledged the existence of Elohim in the first place. Which it doesn't; to Werewolf, Demon might as well just not exist.<br /> <br /> Mummies are all over the place. They facilitated a mega-crossover in Ancient Egypt, but that probably wouldn't fly with the lore as it is now. Would likely also be seen as an affront to life, albeit more in a confused manner than a &quot;kill it yesterday&quot; vampire kind of manner.<br /> <br /> Some Changers will hate certain groups more or less. Silent Striders and Mokole are well known for being extra willing to summary execute every vampire they encounter, for example, with the latter far more exuberant about it due to their ties to the sun. Corax also harbor a distaste for vampires, but they're more likely to listen in and then use the 78 degrees and sunny grenade later. Most non-Fianna and non-Ceilican tend to be so confused about changelings as to not care. Some tribes and types of Fera can speak to the dead more readily than others.<br /> <br /> Finally, Mage's word on crossover tends to, in the words of Team Four Star, make a lot of assumptions, with the first being that most monsters don't want to kill mages horribly. This is generally not the case. Even Akashics and Stargazers don't actually have a peaceful relationship of allies; at best, it's extremely tense and saying the wrong thing could make it blow up at any moment..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T09:53:08-08:00","id":389962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=389894#post389894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Akashics and Stargazers don't actually have a peaceful relationship of allies; at best, it's extremely tense and saying the wrong thing could make it blow up at any moment..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly right. I think the Akashic book says basically.. &quot;generally avoid them, but if they ask for our help we should give it fully&quot;. Definitely would be easy to explode that old alliance if the ancient Akashic masters don't get involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:16:21-08:00","id":390653,"title":"","content":"Relationships... ...Well, all the others simply be Jelly of the Mages.<br /> I think that sounds about right...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:32:21-08:00","id":390698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=389894#post389894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, Mage's word on crossover tends to, in the words of Team Four Star, make a lot of assumptions, with the first being that most monsters don't want to kill mages horribly. This is generally not the case. Even Akashics and Stargazers don't actually have a peaceful relationship of allies; at best, it's extremely tense and saying the wrong thing could make it blow up at any moment..</div> </div> </div> </div>That was only a thing in Revised, the original Stargazer book had praises to the Akashics.<br /> <br /> And generally that default antagonism is a Revised thing to avoid crossovers, it is just that of the big three, Mage was the one who tried to make that approach a bit less manichaean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 02-02-2015, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T20:30:14-08:00","id":390920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=390698#post390698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was only a thing in Revised, the original Stargazer book had praises to the Akashics.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those were some dreadful, crossover-happy days indeed. I'm much more interested in how Stargazer Gifts interact with Werewolf than the crossover-help powers that littered that book or the general atmosphere that almost seem poised to terminally poison any chance of having Werewolf played as Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And generally that default antagonism is a Revised thing to avoid crossovers, it is just that of the big three, Mage was the one who tried to make that approach a bit less manichaean. </div> </div> </div>And that's why I preferred revised. Werewolf already has plenty of room for animosity and reconciliation with Fera (or Fera mained while working tenuously and by trial with Garou). Other games, particularly ones that are so at odds with its themes, are probably best left out of the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:28:57-08:00","id":391051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=390653#post390653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relationships... ...Well, all the others simply be Jelly of the Mages.<br /> I think that sounds about right...</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost. I think you meant werewolves make jelly <i>out</i> of the mages, but you were close. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T02:22:21-08:00","id":391173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=390920#post390920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's why I preferred revised. Werewolf already has plenty of room for animosity and reconciliation with Fera (or Fera mained while working tenuously and by trial with Garou). Other games, particularly ones that are so at odds with its themes, are probably best left out of the mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, such extreme line separations always comes across as stupid (usually by throwing an idiot ball to the splats) as the crossover-happy days. Extremes are never good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:08:23-08:00","id":391489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=391173#post391173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day, such extreme line separations always comes across as stupid (usually by throwing an idiot ball to the splats) as the crossover-happy days. Extremes are never good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The crossover-happy days had Haight, so no, the Revised stuff doesn't even register on the scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:38:58-08:00","id":391756,"title":"","content":"In the original tribebooks, the Black Furries have close ties to the Verbana (for understandable reasons), but find the Euthanos Wyrm-tained and deserve to be destroyed (maybe because of their death dealing and Greek roots hit a little too close to home). There's even a Verbana-turned-Marauder that has two Black Furries who pal along with her. (I think her name is Maeda.) And the Children of Gaia also saw potential in the Mages, but find their selfishness a danger to themselves and others (though they believed that the Cult of Ecstasy were the ones that had the most hope going for them.)<br /> <br /> And let's not forget the complex relationship between the Fiana and the Fae (see the revised tribebook).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:42:23-08:00","id":391764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=391756#post391756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original tribebooks, the Black Furries have close ties to the Verbana (for understandable reasons), but find the Euthanos Wyrm-tained and deserve to be destroyed (maybe because of their death dealing and Greek roots hit a little too close to home). There's even a Verbana-turned-Marauder that has two Black Furries who pal along with her. (I think her name is Maeda.) And the Children of Gaia also saw potential in the Mages, but find their selfishness a danger to themselves and others (though they believed that the Cult of Ecstasy were the ones that had the most hope going for them.)<br /> <br /> And let's not forget the complex relationship between the Fiana and the Fae (see the revised tribebook).</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Umbra had more about Garou- and Fera-fae relations. Essentially, it's a crap shoot, and betrayals are frequent, particularly where the Dreaming connects with the Umbra (which are also places that Garou and Fera can use to basically batter their way into a locale a short way into the Dreaming and knock in heads if it becomes necessary).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:43:04-08:00","id":391872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=391489#post391489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The crossover-happy days had Haight, so no, the Revised stuff doesn't even register on the scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haight was first edition early second, that was a whole new level even in the crossover-happy days. Also, at the point he was absurdly over-templated he was already kind of a joke.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T06:55:18-08:00","id":392566,"title":"","content":"I honestly thought Samuel Haight was White Wolf making fun of their powergaming players. Was that not the case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T07:04:18-08:00","id":392570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=392566#post392566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly thought Samuel Haight was White Wolf making fun of their powergaming players. Was that not the case?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was playing when Sam Haight became a thing, and that is absolutely how it felt at the time. In fact, it was so over the top that it sort of helped us shut down snowflake concepts by saying... &quot;oh, shit that sounds cool. So is this Bob Haight, Sam's cousin-brother?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T07:42:30-08:00","id":392583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=391051#post391051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Almost. I think you meant werewolves make jelly <i>out</i> of the mages, but you were close. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The Werewolf only thought he had made the Mage into Jelly but when it is all down he finds that he was Jelly All along...<br /> <br /> Just as Planned...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T09:21:11-08:00","id":392647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=391756#post391756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original tribebooks, the Black Furries have close ties to the Verbana (for understandable reasons), but find the Euthanos Wyrm-tained and deserve to be destroyed (maybe because of their death dealing and Greek roots hit a little too close to home).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because the Euthanatos get cast as modern ooky-spooky zombie-raising corpse-loving necromancers, partially due to the naming and portrayal of their Specialty Sphere as &quot;Entropy&quot; and partly because that's a slot that us modern people have in our heads as a fantasy trope that needs filling. It really has nothing to do with what Greek Euthanatos should probably be like. Why would Greek Verbena be okay to Black Furies and Greek Euthanatos not be? They might even be hard to tell apart.... I follow the Cycle of Life &amp; Death, Winter &amp; Summer through the Orphic/Elysian mysteries is one major paradigm for both. <br /> <br /> Also, having a primary Sphere of Entropy, when Entropy means WYRM in Werewolf ends up in equating Euthanatos as Wyrm-tainted. Verbena have Life and Life is GOOD. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T10:01:16-08:00","id":392665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=392647#post392647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because the Euthanatos get cast as modern ooky-spooky zombie-raising corpse-loving necromancers, partially due to the naming and portrayal of their Specialty Sphere as &quot;Entropy&quot; and partly because that's a slot that us modern people have in our heads as a fantasy trope that needs filling. It really has nothing to do with what Greek Euthanatos should probably be like. Why would Greek Verbena be okay to Black Furies and Greek Euthanatos not be? They might even be hard to tell apart.... I follow the Cycle of Life &amp; Death, Winter &amp; Summer through the Orphic/Elysian mysteries is one major paradigm for both.<br /> <br /> Also, having a primary Sphere of Entropy, when Entropy means WYRM in Werewolf ends up in equating Euthanatos as Wyrm-tainted. Verbena have Life and Life is GOOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also mentioned in the Euthanatos Tradition Book how they find a bit hypocritical how some Garou call them Wyrm-tained for the occasional Jhor to then indulge themselves into their usual blood-thirst and rage shenanigans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T01:42:45-08:00","id":393528,"title":"","content":"The Euthanatos trad book is pretty damn good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T03:18:45-08:00","id":393603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=393528#post393528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Euthanatos trad book is pretty damn good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is, both are actually.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T12:53:21-08:00","id":394050,"title":"","content":"The movie came out way after my gaming groups had scattered to the four winds, but <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0403358/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Night Watch</i></a> made me think it would be fun to have a crossover game for all the supernatural types that did away with their normal clan/sect/tribe/tradition organizations and had everyone's allegiances based on general philosophy rather than splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T00:30:44-08:00","id":394571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=394050#post394050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The movie came out way after my gaming groups had scattered to the four winds, but <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0403358/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Night Watch</i></a> made me think it would be fun to have a crossover game for all the supernatural types that did away with their normal clan/sect/tribe/tradition organizations and had everyone's allegiances based on general philosophy rather than splat.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why do you love &quot;\u041d\u043e\u0447\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u0414\u043e\u0437\u043e\u0440&quot; so much, people?! In Russia practically no one likes it, saying that books are way, way better. Colloquiially it is known as &quot;\u041d\u043e\u0447\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u041f\u043e\u0437\u043e\u0440&quot; (&quot;Night Shame&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T06:43:31-08:00","id":394741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=394571#post394571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Why do you love &quot;\u041d\u043e\u0447\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u0414\u043e\u0437\u043e\u0440&quot; so much, people?! In Russia practically no one likes it, saying that books are way, way better. Colloquiially it is known as &quot;\u041d\u043e\u0447\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u041f\u043e\u0437\u043e\u0440&quot; (&quot;Night Shame&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it is refreshing to see a non-american (or in this case non-western) take on a genre, especially involving mythology.<br /> Nightwatch had certain style and sensibilities that couldn't come out of hollywood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T14:26:46-07:00","id":1558754,"title":"","content":"<b>I</b> know that this is an old topic, but I felt like what I wanted to bring up fit best here, rather than in a new thread. This is conjecture on My part, and I'd love to know if people agree or disagree, and why they agree or disagree. The point isn't to have a stupid argument, but to examine the pros and cons of My thoughts on the matter at hand, to fairly assess them beyond &quot;I think this works&quot;. <br /> In <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b>, in the section about Greece, it states that the Black Furies are distrustful of the Amenti because of their prior dealings with the Cabiri. On the other hand, I have looked thorugh more sourcebooks than I can count, and I never once read anything, anywhere, about the Black Furies dealing with the Cabiri. The closest thing that I've found, I admit, is a stretch.<br /> In the <b>Revised Edition Tribebook: Black Furies</b>, it is stated that the Black Furies have previously encountered Wyrm-tainted wizards, in Greece, who turned themselves into immortals. When you read the <b>Revised Edition Traditionbook: Euthanatos</b>, it's stated, not only (surprisingly) that the Euthanatos approve of mummies, but that many of the Cabiri had once been Euthanatos (or at least pre-Euthanatoi). Given that Euthanatos with Jhor pick up on Sense Wyrm, I figured that this might be the Wyrm-tainted wizards with whom they had to contend, and that if many of the Cabiri had been from among their number, this would explain, perfectly, the Black Furies having had prior dealings with the Cabiri that make them distrustful of any other of the Undying (beyond, you know, being Garou, and nearly all Garou who even know that mummies are a thing seeing mummies as a blasphemous affront to Gaia). <br /> I know that this is a stretch. Can anyone explain why I might be completely off-base, and perhaps offer a better explanation for the bad dealings between the Black Furies and the Cabiri?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23923-lord-vil","name":"Lord Vil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23923_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T13:09:17-07:00","id":1558802,"title":"","content":"I think that &quot;dealing with the Cabiri&quot; is just the natural result of some tribal identities proceeding them to the sensibilities of authors. They see &quot;Greek werewolves&quot; and auto-file it with everything else, like satyrs from Changeling, though those two at least have some history of interaction, since the fae used to be more common and satyrs were probably drawn to Garou because they appreciate passion and what else is Rage?<br /> <br /> Mummies, though? They like to stay hidden, not go playing with anyone who could potentially send them into the Underworld ahead of schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T14:45:22-07:00","id":1558806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Vil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/389504-supernatural-relations?p=1558754#post1558754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I</b> know that this is an old topic, but I felt like what I wanted to bring up fit best here, rather than in a new thread. This is conjecture on My part, and I'd love to know if people agree or disagree, and why they agree or disagree. The point isn't to have a stupid argument, but to examine the pros and cons of My thoughts on the matter at hand, to fairly assess them beyond &quot;I think this works&quot;.<br /> In <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b>, in the section about Greece, it states that the Black Furies are distrustful of the Amenti because of their prior dealings with the Cabiri. On the other hand, I have looked thorugh more sourcebooks than I can count, and I never once read anything, anywhere, about the Black Furies dealing with the Cabiri. The closest thing that I've found, I admit, is a stretch.<br /> In the <b>Revised Edition Tribebook: Black Furies</b>, it is stated that the Black Furies have previously encountered Wyrm-tainted wizards, in Greece, who turned themselves into immortals. When you read the <b>Revised Edition Traditionbook: Euthanatos</b>, it's stated, not only (surprisingly) that the Euthanatos approve of mummies, but that many of the Cabiri had once been Euthanatos (or at least pre-Euthanatoi). Given that Euthanatos with Jhor pick up on Sense Wyrm, I figured that this might be the Wyrm-tainted wizards with whom they had to contend, and that if many of the Cabiri had been from among their number, this would explain, perfectly, the Black Furies having had prior dealings with the Cabiri that make them distrustful of any other of the Undying (beyond, you know, being Garou, and nearly all Garou who even know that mummies are a thing seeing mummies as a blasphemous affront to Gaia).<br /> I know that this is a stretch. Can anyone explain why I might be completely off-base, and perhaps offer a better explanation for the bad dealings between the Black Furies and the Cabiri?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the fact that, as you mentioned, being hostile to something like the Cabiri would tend to be the default position for most Garou, there's some other reasons worth considering. The Black Furies are one of the Tribes more closely aligned with the Wyld, which might make them particular hostile to something they see as unnatural. It's also worth mentioning that the works of Cabirus are also associated with one of the paths to Lichedom in Mage; they could also be the Wyrm-tainted wizards in question, or even a combination of the two if they also dealt with some of the nastier Cabiri on occasion.<br /> <br /> It's also not too surprising that proto-Euthanatoi/Chakravanti, or at least some of them, would take a favourable view of Mummies. To the extent that Mummies abide by a cycle of life and death of sorts, they can probably integrate it into their philosophies as a form of reincarnation (in contrast to the unnatural stasis of a Liche). Idran Mages researching necrosynthesis, the fusion of life and death, is what led to the creation of the Nagaraja. <br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> is probably right that a lot of this is just the authors going with the easy default relationship for two groups associated with the same region of the world, without really putting much thought into it. From what I recall hearing, collaboration between the writers on different game lines in later years tended to be spotty at best. I haven't read the relevant source material, so I can't really say anything for sure, but your thoughts on the matter seem to do a decent job of adding some connective tissue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}